@base = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@kc = http://localhost:8180/realms/room-booking

### OIDC discovery document
GET {{kc}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

### Provider public keys (JWKS)
GET {{kc}}/protocol/openid-connect/certs

### Token for alice (password grant – demo only; real clients use Authorization Code + PKCE)
# @name alice
POST {{kc}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=room-booking-cli&username=alice&password=alice-password&scope=openid

### Call the API with the Keycloak token (user provisioned on first call)
GET {{base}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.access_token}}

### Book as alice
POST {{base}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"roomId": "0199a3f0-0000-7000-8000-000000000002", "startTime": "2026-10-12T09:00:00Z", "endTime": "2026-10-12T10:00:00Z"}

### Token for bob (roles USER + ADMIN)
# @name bob
POST {{kc}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=room-booking-cli&username=bob&password=bob-password

###
GET {{base}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.access_token}}

### Token issued for another client (no room-booking-api audience) -> 401
# @name other
POST {{kc}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=admin-cli&username=alice&password=alice-password

###
GET {{base}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{other.response.body.access_token}}
